        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "(Apparently part of the lower half of a natural-colored linen bedspread of which the Chicago Art Institute has the upper half: 48.155); fragmentary design worked with yellow, coral pink, gray, blue and a little black silk (black now mostly rotted out) in chain stitch with some satin stitch; figure on horseback blowing a horn; man leading a dog (?); striped snakes; highly ornamental animals and the word FAMA underneath the rider."@en ;
